# {{name}}

A CLI that generates a fully configured trading agent from a plain-English strategy.

## What Is This

This project runs a LangChain trading agent on Base using your selected wallet/provider setup.

## Configuration

| Setting | Value |
|---------|-------|
| Network | Base Mainnet (8453) |
| Wallet | {{wallet}} |
| LLM | {{model}} |
| Test mode | {{testMode}} |
| Tools | {{#each selectedToolNames}}{{this}}{{#unless @last}}, {{/unless}}{{/each}}{{#unless hasAnyTools}}none{{/unless}} |

## Requirements

- Node.js 20+
- A funded wallet for live trading
- `.env` credentials
- Base mainnet funding for gas + trading capital

## Setup

```bash
npm i
# .env is already created by the scaffolder
# fill in any missing wallet/provider keys
```

{{#if isBankr}}
## Bankr API Key Setup

1. Create your key at `bankr.bot`.
2. Turn **Read Only** OFF.
3. Set `BANKR_API_KEY` in `.env`.

If Read Only is ON, execution calls will fail with auth/permission errors.
{{/if}}

{{#if isCdpServerWallet}}
## CDP Server Wallet Key Setup

1. Create CDP API credentials in `portal.cdp.coinbase.com` and copy:
   - `CDP_API_KEY_ID`
   - `CDP_API_KEY_SECRET`
2. Create/copy your **Wallet Auth Key** (base64 secret) and set `CDP_WALLET_SECRET`.
3. Use ECDSA-compatible credentials for trading SDK compatibility.

`CDP_WALLET_SECRET` is different from `CDP_API_KEY_SECRET`.
{{/if}}

{{#if isSponge}}
## Sponge API Key Setup

1. Register at `https://paysponge.com/`.
2. Create a `SPONGE_API_KEY`.
3. Set `SPONGE_API_KEY` in `.env`.

Sponge handles wallet execution natively for swaps, bridging, Polymarket, Hyperliquid, and related flows.
{{/if}}

{{#if hasVirtuals}}
## Virtuals ACP Setup

1. Install the ACP CLI from `https://github.com/Virtual-Protocol/openclaw-acp`.
2. Run `acp setup` once to authenticate and provision the agent wallet/profile.
3. Leave `VIRTUALS_ACP_BIN=acp` in `.env`, or point it at a different ACP executable path.

The built-in `virtuals` tool exposes ACP marketplace browsing, job creation, job status checks, and wallet balance lookup for helper-agent delegation.
{{/if}}

## Running The Agent

```bash
npm start
```

On first start, the agent prints:
- Wallet identity (`[WALLET] ...`)
- Current funding status (`[BALANCE] ...`)
- A funding warning + short poll loop if balances are missing
- Strategy preview and a `[READY]` prompt

## Interacting With The Agent

Type plain-English messages at any time while it is running:
- `"be more conservative with position size"`
- `"focus only on ETH/USDC today"`
- `"pause execution unless setup is high conviction"`

Your input is injected into the next cycle as a high-priority user directive; pressing Enter also wakes the loop early.

## Terminal Output

Each cycle is rendered in a compact structure:
- `STATUS`
- `ACTION`
- `RATIONALE`

When transaction hashes are detected, Basescan links are printed automatically.

The agent should never claim a trade succeeded unless it has a verified transaction hash.

## Strategy + Guardrails

- Strategy source: `prompts/strategy.md`
- Guardrails source: `src/guardrails.ts`
- Generated guardrail defaults:
  - Slippage tolerance: {{guardrails.slippagePct}}%
  - Stop-loss threshold: {{guardrails.stopLossPct}}%
  - Max position size: {{guardrails.maxPositionPct}}% of wallet
  - Absolute per-trade cap: `MAX_TRADE_USD` (default $100)

### What is enforced in code

`src/guardrails.ts` classifies every tool before the agent sees it (default-deny). Built-in
read-only tools{{#if hasAnyX402}} and the x402 paid-data tools (whose payments are capped, see below){{/if}}{{#if hasNansenMcp}} and the Nansen MCP analytics tools{{/if}} are
not wrapped. Tools with a built-in policy are checked on every call. Every other tool, including
MCP and custom tools, is blocked unless the operator lists it in `GUARDRAIL_ALLOW_TOOLS`. A
blocked call returns a JSON error (`{"success":false,"error":"[guardrail] Blocked ..."}`) to
the model and logs a `[guardrail] Blocked ...` line; the agent loop keeps running.

- **Arbitrary destinations are blocked by default.** {{#if isCdpServerWallet}}`cdp_send_transaction`, `cdp_contract_write`, and `cdp_transfer`{{/if}}{{#if isSponge}}`sponge_transfer_evm` and transfer steps in `sponge_submit_plan`{{/if}}{{#if isBankr}}`bankr_execute` (when enabled) prompts with transfer/withdraw/approve/bridge intent{{/if}}{{#if hasVirtuals}}, plus `virtuals_create_job`,{{/if}} only run when the destination is in `ALLOWED_ADDRESSES` (comma-separated, case-insensitive; empty by default).
{{#if isCdpServerWallet}}
- **Raw calls are decoded.** Allowlisting a contract does not grant arbitrary execution on it. `cdp_send_transaction`/`cdp_contract_write` calldata must decode to ERC-20 `transfer`/`transferFrom`/`approve` or ERC-721/1155 `setApprovalForAll`/`safeTransferFrom`/`transferFrom`, and the decoded recipient/spender/operator and amount must pass the same policies as the dedicated tools (recipients and operators in `ALLOWED_ADDRESSES`; spenders allowlisted or a hardcoded protocol router; stablecoin amounts capped by `MAX_TRADE_USD` using the token's real decimals). Unrecognized calldata, multicall/nested calls, and permit/Permit2 calls are rejected. `increaseAllowance` is always rejected (even with `ALLOW_ARBITRARY_CALLDATA=true`); use `approve` with the exact amount. `ALLOW_ARBITRARY_CALLDATA=true` lifts this and grants **unrestricted execution authority** on allowlisted targets.
- **Approvals.** Every approval path (`cdp_erc20_approve`, protocol approval helpers{{#if hasUniswap}}, approvals returned by the Uniswap API{{/if}}, and decoded approval calldata) checks the final encoded amount: unlimited (>= 2^255, including maxUint256) is rejected, stablecoin approvals are capped by `MAX_TRADE_USD`, and the spender must be a router hardcoded by the generated protocol tools or in `ALLOWED_ADDRESSES`{{#if hasUniswap}}. Unlimited Uniswap API approvals are re-encoded as exact-amount approvals before the check{{/if}}.
- **Fixed-router protocol tools** ({{#if hasUniswap}}Uniswap, {{/if}}{{#if hasAerodrome}}Aerodrome, {{/if}}{{#if hasAvantis}}Avantis, {{/if}}`cdp_swap`) keep working without an allowlist.
{{/if}}
- **Slippage.** Slippage inputs on swap/perp tools are clamped to `SLIPPAGE_PCT`.
- **Trade size.** `MAX_TRADE_USD` caps tool inputs that are USD/stablecoin-denominated (stablecoin swap/transfer amounts, whether the token is given by symbol or address{{#if hasAvantis}}, Avantis collateral, margin deposits and USDC approvals{{/if}}{{#if isSponge}}, Sponge Hyperliquid size and Polymarket amount{{/if}}{{#if isBankr}}, `$`/USDC amounts found in Bankr prompts{{/if}}). Token amounts are converted with the same token registry and decimals the protocol tools use. `MAX_POSITION_PCT` is also enforced for those inputs when the wallet adapter reports a USD total ({{#if isCdpServerWallet}}not available for the CDP wallet{{else}}Bankr/Sponge balances{{/if}}).
{{#if isSponge}}
- **Sponge plans.** `sponge_submit_plan` accepts only `swap` and `transfer` steps with known params; each step is checked with the same policy as `sponge_swap_base` / `sponge_transfer_evm`. `sponge_approve_plan` only approves plan IDs that this agent process submitted and the guardrails accepted.
- **Paid proxy fetches.** `sponge_x402_fetch` only pays hosts listed in `ALLOWED_X402_HOSTS`.
{{/if}}
{{#if isBankr}}
- **Bankr execution is disabled by default.** `bankr_execute` is blocked unless `BANKR_ALLOW_EXECUTE=true`. When enabled it is effectively unrestricted; only best-effort prompt checks apply. `bankr_get_balances` stays available.
{{/if}}
{{#if hasAnyX402}}
- **x402 payments.** The shared x402 client only pays the built-in data hosts (plus `ALLOWED_X402_HOSTS`), only in USDC on Base, and at most `MAX_X402_PAYMENT_USD` (default 0.10) per request. Redirects are never followed (any 3xx is an error), so an allowed host cannot forward a request or payment elsewhere.
{{/if}}
{{#if hasAgentcashMcp}}
- **AgentCash MCP tools** have no built-in policy, so they are blocked until you list the ones you trust in `GUARDRAIL_ALLOW_TOOLS` (they then run unchecked).
{{/if}}

### What is not enforced

- Trades whose input amount is not USD-denominated (for example selling ETH or another volatile token) have no USD cap; the scaffold does not price tokens.
- `STOP_LOSS_PCT` is strategy guidance; the scaffold does not monitor positions and exit automatically.
{{#if isBankr}}
- With `BANKR_ALLOW_EXECUTE=true`, Bankr checks are best-effort pattern matching on the prompt, not a guarantee.
{{/if}}
- Tools listed in `GUARDRAIL_ALLOW_TOOLS` run without any checks.
- Leverage is not capped.

### Loosening the guardrails

These are operator controls. You can loosen them by adding addresses to `ALLOWED_ADDRESSES`, raising or disabling `MAX_TRADE_USD` (`unlimited`), raising `SLIPPAGE_PCT`/`MAX_POSITION_PCT`, listing tools in `GUARDRAIL_ALLOW_TOOLS`{{#if isCdpServerWallet}}, setting `ALLOW_ARBITRARY_CALLDATA=true`{{/if}}{{#if isBankr}}, setting `BANKR_ALLOW_EXECUTE=true`{{/if}}{{#if hasAnyX402}}, raising `MAX_X402_PAYMENT_USD`{{/if}}, or editing `src/guardrails.ts`. Every change widens what an agent acting on untrusted tool output can do with your funds.
{{#if isSelfUpdating}}

### Self-updating strategy

Every `EVALUATION_INTERVAL_MINUTES`, the agent may propose a new strategy. By default the proposal is written to `prompts/strategy.proposed.md` and logged; it is **not** used as the system prompt until you review it and copy it into `prompts/strategy.md`. Set `AUTO_APPLY_STRATEGY_UPDATES=true` to apply proposals automatically (recorded in `strategy-history.json`).
{{/if}}
